    "Description": "Red Hat OpenStack Platform provides the facilities for building, deploying and monitoring a private or public infrastructure-as-a-service (IaaS) cloud running on commonly available physical hardware.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* golang: crypto/x509: Man-in-the-middle attacks via untrusted intermediate\ncertificates (CVE-2026-111943)\n\n* net/url: Memory exhaustion in query parameter parsing in net/url\n(CVE-2025-61726)\n\n* Incorrect parsing of IPv6 host literals in net/url (CVE-2026-25679)\n\n* golang: golang crypto/x509: Denial of Service via excessive processing of\nDNS SAN entries (CVE-2026-27145)\n\n* crypto/tls: golang: Go: Denial of Service vulnerability in certificate\nchain building (CVE-2026-32280)\n\n* golang: Go crypto/tls: Denial of Service via multiple TLS 1.3 key update\nmessages (CVE-2026-32283)\n\n* golang: Go net package: Denial of Service via long CNAME response in\nLookupCNAME (CVE-2026-33811)\n\n* golang: Go encoding/asn1: Denial of Service via excessive recursion in\nUnmarshal (CVE-2026-33818)\n\n* golang: net/http: golang.org/x/net/idna: Privilege escalation via\nincorrect Punycode label processing (CVE-2026-39821)\n\n* golang: Go net/http: Unencrypted HTTP/2 connections vulnerable to Denial\nof Service (CVE-2026-56853)\n\n* golang: Go html/template: Cross-Site Scripting via pathological input\n(CVE-2026-56858)\n\n* golang: golang net/url: Denial of Service from quadratic complexity in\npath resolution (CVE-2026-56860)\n\n* golang: Golang crypto/tls: Denial of Service via indefinite KeyUpdate\nmessages (CVE-2026-56862)\n\n* etcd: Denial of Service via unbounded TLS handshake goroutines\n(CVE-2026-73500)\n\n* net/http/internal/http2: golang.org/x/net/http2: net/http: Denial of\nService via excessive HTTP/2 SETTINGS frames (CVE-2026-78669)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page listed in the References section.",
